  "ai_language_tip": "Speak clear, polite standard Slovak (sk); Czech is widely understood; Hungarian is used in parts of the south; English works in Bratislava, Tatras resorts and hotels, less at clinics and offices.",
  "english_ok": "sometimes — Fair in Bratislava, mountain resorts and hotels and with younger staff; scarce at state clinics, municipal offices and villages.",
  "politeness": "Formal 'vykanie' (vy), 'pán/pani' + surname; open with 'Dobrý deň' and state on whose behalf; close with 'Ďakujem, dovidenia'.",
  "name_tip": "Surname first; female surnames take -ová (Kováč / Kováčová); give the exact form and spell foreign names letter by letter.",
  "phone_tip": "Mobile 09xx xxx xxx (10 digits with 0), Bratislava landline 02 + 8 digits, +421 country code; SMS confirmations common.",
  "time_tip": "TRAP: 'pol ôsmej' = 7:30, 'štvrť na osem' = 7:15, 'trištvrte na osem' = 7:45; always read back in 24h.",
  "number_tip": "People are counted with special forms ('dvaja', 'traja', 'štyria' for men/mixed groups); 3-izbový = 3-room flat, not party size; read phones in groups.",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid lunch rush 11:30–13:30 (obedové menu), dinner peak 18:30–20:30, calls after 20:00 and weekends for offices; GP surgeries answer mostly in the morning.",
  "closed_days": "Shops open Sundays; since 1 November 2025 retail must close only on 1 January, Good Friday, Easter Sunday, 24 December after 12:00 and 25–26 December; days of rest include 6 January, Easter Monday, 1 May, 5 July, 29 August, 1 November, 24–26 December, while 1 September, 28 October and 17 November are no longer days off (8 May and 15 September also suspended in 2026).",
